00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
you know for all of the fear-mongering  about democrats  really being socialists obama was a  marxist  bernie is a communist all of this stuff  you've been seeing it for years  is it possible that donald trump is the  most  socialist president that we've ever had  or at least  in decades you know we did a story a  year or two ago  about is donald trump the first atheist  president we talked about other  non-religious presidents or  presidents believed to be non-religious  and  we talked about the reality that donald  trump appears to be lying about being  religious  just to try to placate evangelical  voters  it doesn't make trump a better president  not to be religious but he just might  not be  religious despite his claims that he  loves the bible and all of this stuff  well what about trump as a socialist  president now to be clear  trump is not a socialist but we are  talking here about  the the sort of haphazard definition of  socialism and communism  that the right likes to wrongly ascribe  to the ideas of the left  but there is a long list of the  socialization of some elements of the  economy by donald trump  that could arguably make trump the  closest thing we've had  to the definition of a socialist  president that his  supporters tend to ascribe to socialism  now  you know to be clear there's socialism  and then there's sort of like social  democracy that is sometimes called  socialism  i understand that but let's consider  this and use the spectrum because that's  really what it is  in terms of government stimulus which  the right  loves to call socialism the first  coronavirus relief package was 2.2  trillion in the cares act  trillions coming in additional forms  trillions pumped into the market by the  fed  this is way way way bigger than the  obama stimulus which  they called socialist remember obama was  a socialist for an 800 billion dollar  stimulus bill  and for mandating you buy private health  insurance  from for-profit companies bush's bank  bailout  was about 400 billion this is like 8  trillion in total  trump used the defense production act to  force general motors to make ventilators  after initial talks broke down over  costs  this is heavy government involvement in  directing the activities  of private industry something that the  right loves to call  socialism in soviet russia the  government tells you  what kind of bread to make trump  threatened to condition the sale of  tick-tock to microsoft  on the u.s receiving a very big  portion of the sale price and said that  nobody else thinks about deals this way  other than him  straight up saying government will take  a cut  of a private business deal because why  because trump wants a cut  if barack obama had ever suggested  anything like this fox news would have  gone bananas for 10 days  donald trump has massively expanded  direct farm aid from 11 billion in 2017  to more than 32 billion in 2020 all so  he could  pay off the farmers who were hurt by his  trade war he has  socialized a larger portion of  agriculture  than previous presidents when harley  davidson wanted to move some of its  manufacturing over to europe  trump threatened them with regulating  them and taxing them like never before  this is extraordinarily heavy-handed in  terms of a government crackdown on a  business  that the right calls socialists when a  democrat suggests  doing it trump moved to prop up the  local  the uh domestic coal industry  despite the market deciding it's time to  wrap up coal coal doesn't make sense  the government is overriding markets  to decide which industry will succeed or  fail  wow and where is the right on this trump  has also  raised the deficit massively obama left  office  with about a 500 billion deficit  down from 1.5 trillion remember that  deficit not debt  trump doubled where barack obama left  off before coronavirus  and now obviously with coronavirus  everything is completely out of control  the right loves to say those socialist  democrats raise the deficit but it's  trump who's done it historically  trump when asked about debt and deficit  deflects and talks about you know we've  got to build up the military and the  wall  and that's going to help the overall  economy  which is almost like a modern monetary  theory type  argument which is just do the projects  and the economy will benefit except  trump's doing it with the wrong projects  that would make sense to say  you know improving health care and  education in the short run might  increase the deficit  but we will benefit so much that in the  long run it will actually be  deficit negative or deficit neutral  trump's sort of making that argument  but with the wrong things like building  a wall as an example  now trump supporters will say trump  didn't want to do any socialism  but he had to do it because of  coronavirus for the good of the country  and that's true to us  to a certain degree but it's what he did  nonetheless  a true capitalist would have said let  the businesses fail  if you don't want to fly because of a  virus let the airlines go under that's  not what donald trump is doing  it's also the experience of fdr by the  way  i mean he arguably  somewhat reluctantly came to some of the  policies he came to  in order to kind of save capitalism from  itself now  fdr is seen by some as the most  socialist president we've had trump has  arguably done  more presidents have to respond to the  events of their presidency that's for  sure you can't remove coronavirus from  it  sort of like imagining lincoln's  presidency without the civil war  or fdr's presidency without recovering  from the great depression in world war  ii  trump had to deal with coronavirus but  he chose to do it this way it could have  been done other ways  now of course trump has also done other  things that are not  socialistic right he's deregulated  business so business can pollute more  so cars can be less efficient cut  funding to agencies cut  taxes for some people but despite all of  that by many measures  trump could still be the most  socialistic president  in many of our lifetimes you've got to  go back at least to nixon  who created the epa osha boosted  regulation  social security benefits maybe you'd go  back to dwight eisenhower who passed the  interstate highway act  subsidized mortgages and college tuition  had a 91 percent top marginal tax rate  despite  lots of ways to reduce the effective tax  rate what's the reaction from trumpists  absolutely none they're too busy trying  to suppress the vote to actually care  about what it is that donald trump is  doing  weird times we live in my friends

